ign system",[1389,1433,1434,1437],{},[1404,1435,1436],{},"Vite\u002Fwebpack",[1404,1438,1439],{},"Bundling and dev server",[14,1441,1442,1445],{},[638,1443,1444],{},"Modern recommendation",": use CSS variables (runtime theming) + a build tool (Vite) + PostCSS (prefixes\u002Fminification). Add Sass if you need mixins\u002Floops. Add Tailwind if you prefer utility-first.",[18,1447,1449],{"id":1448},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[891,1451,1452,1466,1485,1490,1502],{},[894,1453,1454,1457,1458,1461,1462,1465],{},[638,1455,1456],{},"Idiom",": use CSS variables for theming (runtime, JS-accessible, media-query-responsive) and Sass variables for build-time math\u002Fmixins — they're complementary. ",[26,1459,1460],{},"--primary"," changes at runtime; ",[26,1463,1464],{},"$breakpoint"," is a compile-time constant for loops.",[894,1467,1468,1470,1471,1473,1474,1476,1477,1479,1480,1482,1483,761],{},[638,1469,1456],{},": use ",[26,1472,651],{}," (not ",[26,1475,757],{},") in modern Sass — ",[26,1478,757],{}," is deprecated. ",[26,1481,651],{}," is scoped (no global pollution) and loads once. ",[26,1484,655],{},[894,1486,1487,1489],{},[638,1488,1456],{},": use PostCSS for prefixes and minification (Autoprefixer + cssnano) — it works on standard CSS, composable with other plugins. Vite\u002Fwebpack integrate it; configure once and forget.",[894,1491,1492,1494,1495,1498,1499,949],{},[638,1493,1456],{},": use CSS Modules for scoped component styles in React — ",[26,1496,1497],{},"import styles from '.\u002FButton.module.css'"," gives locally-scoped class names (no collisions, no BEM needed). Popular with React; for Vue, use ",[26,1500,1501],{},"\u003Cstyle scoped>",[894,1503,1504,1506],{},[638,1505,1456],{},": use Vite for new projects — it handles CSS\u002FSCSS\u002FPostCSS out of the box (install the preprocessor, import the file). Dev uses native ES modules (instant startup); production bundles with Rollup. Faster and simpler than webpack for most apps.",[18,1508,1510],{"id":1509},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[891,1512,1513,1532,1547,1570,1580,1592,1604,1624,1641,1647],{},[894,1514,1515,1470,1521,1159,1523,1525,1526,1528,1529,1531],{},[638,1516,1517,1518,1520],{},"Sass ",[26,1519,757],{}," is deprecated",[26,1522,651],{},[26,1524,655],{},". ",[26,1527,757],{}," pollutes the global namespace and loads the file multiple times. ",[26,1530,651],{}," is scoped and loads once.",[894,1533,1534,61,1537,1540,1541,1543,1544,1546],{},[638,1535,1536],{},"Sass variables are compile-time",[26,1538,1539],{},"$primary: blue"," becomes ",[26,1542,1292],{}," in the compiled CSS — it can't change at runtime or in media queries. Use CSS variables (",[26,1545,1460],{},") for runtime theming.",[894,1548,1549,61,1554,1557,1558,1561,1562,1565,1566,1569],{},[638,1550,1551,1553],{},[26,1552,651],{}," namespaces by default",[26,1555,1556],{},"@use 'variables'"," accesses as ",[26,1559,1560],{},"variables.$primary",". Use ",[26,1563,1564],{},"@use 'variables' as *"," for no namespace, or ",[26,1567,1568],{},"@use 'variables' as v"," for a shorter one.",[894,1571,1572,1575,1576,1579],{},[638,1573,1574],{},"CSS Modules need a framework",": CSS Modules work with React\u002FVue\u002FNext.js via the bundler. A plain ",[26,1577,1578],{},".html"," file can't use them (no scoping mechanism).",[894,1581,1582,61,1588,1591],{},[638,1583,1584,1587],{},[26,1585,1586],{},"@apply"," in Tailwind couples to Tailwind",[26,1589,1590],{},"@apply mt-4;"," in a CSS file makes your CSS dependent on Tailwind's utilities. Use sparingly; prefer composing utilities in JSX\u002FHTML.",[894,1593,1594,61,1597,1599,1600,1603],{},[638,1595,1596],{},"PostCSS plugins have config",[26,1598,904],{}," has stages (0-4); stage 2 is a common default. Autoprefixer needs ",[26,1601,1602],{},"browserslist",". Misconfigured plugins can produce unexpected output.",[894,1605,1606,61,1609,1612,1613,1615,1616,1618,1619,1618,1621,1623],{},[638,1607,1608],{},"Order matters in webpack loaders",[26,1610,1611],{},"use: ['style-loader', 'css-loader', 'postcss-loader', 'sass-loader']"," — loaders execute right-to-left. ",[26,1614,1213],{}," first (SCSS→CSS), then ",[26,1617,1217],{},", then ",[26,1620,1221],{},[26,1622,1225],{}," (inject).",[894,1625,1626,61,1629,1632,1633,1635,1636,1638,1639,949],{},[638,1627,1628],{},"Vite preprocessor auto-import",[26,1630,1631],{},"css.preprocessorOptions.scss.additionalData"," prepends to every SCSS file (useful for ",[26,1634,1556],{},"). But it can cause \"already imported\" errors if a file also imports — use ",[26,1637,651],{}," (idempotent) not ",[26,1640,757],{},[894,1642,1643,1646],{},[638,1644,1645],{},"Lightning CSS vs PostCSS",": Lightning CSS is faster (Rust) but has fewer plugins. PostCSS has a richer ecosystem. Tailwind 4 uses Lightning CSS; many setups still use PostCSS.",[894,1648,1649,1652],{},[638,1650,1651],{},"Minification can change behavior",": aggressive minification (shortening class names, removing \"unused\" CSS) can break things if it misidentifies used classes (dynamic class names in JS). Configure carefully.",[18,1654,1656],{"id":1655},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1658,1659],{},"A developer uses a Sass variable for the primary color and a media query to change it, but the color doesn't change on smaller screens:",[31,1661,1662],{"language":33},[35,1663,1665],{"className":37,"code":1664,"language":33,"meta":39,"style":39},"$primary: blue;\n\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    $primary: red;\n}\n\n.button { background: $primary; }\n",[26,1666,1667,1677,1681,1701,1713,1717,1721],{"__ignoreMap":39},[43,1668,1669,1671,1673,1675],{"class":45,"line":46},[43,1670,57],{"class":56},[43,1672,61],{"class":60},[43,1674,1292],{"class":64},[43,1676,68],{"class":60},[43,1678,1679],{"class":45,"line":53},[43,1680,92],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":91},[43,1682,1683,1686,1689,1692,1694,1697,1699],{"class":45,"line":71},[43,1684,1685],{"class":82},"@media",[43,1687,1688],{"class":60}," (",[43,1690,1691],{"class":64},"max-width",[43,1693,61],{"class":60},[43,1695,1696],{"class":64},"768",[43,1698,377],{"class":82},[43,1700,359],{"class":60},[43,1702,1703,1706,1708,1711],{"class":45,"line":88},[43,1704,1705],{"class":56},"    $primary",[43,1707,61],{"class":60},[43,1709,1710],{"class":64},"red",[43,1712,68],{"class":60},[43,1714,1715],{"class":45,"line":95},[43,1716,221],{"class":60},[43,1718,1719],{"class":45,"line":101},[43,1720,92],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":91},[43,1722,1723,1726,1728,1730,1732,1734],{"class":45,"line":111},[43,1724,1725],{"class":104},".button",[43,1727,406],{"class":60},[43,1729,1287],{"class":64},[43,1731,61],{"class":60},[43,1733,57],{"class":56},[43,1735,498],{"class":60},[14,1737,1738],{},"What's wrong?",[1740,1741,1742,1746,1778,1781,1800,1812,1815,1904,1915],"details",{},[1743,1744,1745],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1747,1748,1749,1752,1753,1755,1756,1759,1760,1764,1765,1768,1769,1771,1772,1774,1775,1777],{},"Sass variables are ",[638,1750,1751],{},"compile-time"," — the ",[26,1754,1685],{}," block's ",[26,1757,1758],{},"$primary: red"," changes the variable's value ",[1761,1762,1763],"em",{},"during compilation",", but only within that block's scope. By the time ",[26,1766,1767],{},".button { background: $primary; }"," is compiled, ",[26,1770,57],{}," is ",[26,1773,1292],{}," (the last assignment in the main scope, outside the ",[26,1776,1685],{}," block).",[14,1779,1780],{},"The compiled CSS is:",[35,1782,1784],{"className":1246,"code":1783,"language":1243,"meta":39,"style":39},".button { background: blue; }\n",[26,1785,1786],{"__ignoreMap":39},[43,1787,1788,1790,1792,1794,1796,1798],{"class":45,"line":46},[43,1789,1725],{"class":104},[43,1791,406],{"class":60},[43,1793,1287],{"class":64},[43,1795,61],{"class":60},[43,1797,1292],{"class":64},[43,1799,498],{"class":60},[14,1801,1802,1803,1805,1806,1808,1809,1811],{},"There's no media query — the ",[26,1804,1758],{}," inside ",[26,1807,1685],{}," didn't persist outside it (Sass ",[26,1810,1685],{}," blocks have their own scope for variables), and even if it did, it's compile-time, so you can't have a different value at a different viewport.",[14,1813,1814],{},"The fix — use CSS variables (runtime, media-query-responsive):",[35,1816,1818],{"className":37,"code":1817,"language":33,"meta":39,"style":39},":root {\n    --primary: blue;\n}\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    :root {\n        --primary: red;\n    }\n}\n.button { background: var(--primary); }\n",[26,1819,1820,1827,1838,1842,1858,1865,1876,1880,1884],{"__ignoreMap":39},[43,1821,1822,1825],{"class":45,"line":46},[43,1823,1824],{"class":104},":root",[43,1826,108],{"class":60},[43,1828,1829,1832,1834,1836],{"class":45,"line":53},[43,1830,1831],{"class":56},"    --primary",[43,1833,61],{"class":60},[43,1835,1292],{"class":64},[43,1837,68],{"class":60},[43,1839,1840],{"class":45,"line":71},[43,1841,221],{"class":60},[43,1843,1844,1846,1848,1850,1852,1854,1856],{"class":45,"line":88},[43,1845,1685],{"class":82},[43,1847,1688],{"class":60},[43,1849,1691],{"class":64},[43,1851,61],{"class":60},[43,1853,1696],{"class":64},[43,1855,377],{"class":82},[43,1857,359],{"class":60},[43,1859,1860,1863],{"class":45,"line":95},[43,1861,1862],{"class":104},"    :root",[43,1864,108],{"class":60},[43,1866,1867,1870,1872,1874],{"class":45,"line":101},[43,1868,1869],{"class":56},"        --primary",[43,1871,61],{"class":60},[43,1873,1710],{"class":64},[43,1875,68],{"class":60},[43,1877,1878],{"class":45,"line":111},[43,1879,183],{"class":60},[43,1881,1882],{"class":45,"line":123},[43,1883,221],{"class":60},[43,1885,1886,1888,1890,1892,1894,1897,1899,1901],{"class":45,"line":136},[43,1887,1725],{"class":104},[43,1889,406],{"class":60},[43,1891,1287],{"class":64},[43,1893,61],{"class":60},[43,1895,1896],{"class":64},"var",[43,1898,353],{"class":60},[43,1900,1460],{"class":56},[43,1902,1903],{"class":60},"); }\n",[14,1905,1906,1907,1771,1909,1911,1912,1914],{},"Now ",[26,1908,1460],{},[26,1910,1292],{}," on desktop and ",[26,1913,1710],{}," on mobile (≤768px), at runtime. The browser applies the right value based on the viewport.",[14,1916,1917,1920,1921,1923],{},[638,1918,1919],{},"The lesson",": Sass variables are compile-time constants — they can't change at runtime or per media query. Use CSS variables (",[26,1922,632],{},") for runtime theming and media-query-responsive values. Use Sass variables only for build-time math, loops, and mixins.",[18,1925,1926],{"id":1743},"Summary",[14,1928,1929,1930,1159,1932,1934,1935,1937],{},"You know Sass (variables, nesting, mixins, functions, loops, ",[26,1931,651],{},[26,1933,655],{},"), Less, Stylus, PostCSS (Autoprefixer, preset-env, cssnano), build tools (Vite, webpack, Lightning CSS), and CSS Modules — and when to use CSS variables (runtime) vs Sass variables (compile-time), with the ",[26,1936,1685],{},"-can't-change-Sass-variable trap avoided. Next: exercises and projects.",[1939,1940,1941],"style",{},"html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-git